   30 T:0000                                    ;
   31 T:0000                                    ; Applesoft BASIC, V2
   32 T:0000                                    ;
   33 T:0000                                    ; Written by Marc McDonald and Randy Wigginton.
   34 T:0000                                    ;
   35 T:0000                                    ; Original copyright 1976 by Microsoft,
   36 T:0000                                    ; 1977 by Apple Computer.
   37 T:0000                                    ;
   38 T:0000                                    ; Disassembled by (unknown).
   39 T:0000                                    ; Fixed by Chris Mosher.
   40 T:0000                                    ; 
   41 T:0000                                    ; For the cc65.org Assembler (ca65)
   42 T:0000                                    ;
   43 T:0000                                    ; Applesoft BASIC was first written by
   44 T:0000                                    ; Marc McDonald, the first employee of Microsoft,
   45 T:0000                                    ; in mid-1976. That version was bought by Apple
   46 T:0000                                    ; and released (on casette) in Nov. 1977.
   47 T:0000                                    ;
   48 T:0000                                    ; Version 2 was written by Randy Wigginton and
   49 T:0000                                    ; others at Apple in spring 1978. This version
   50 T:0000                                    ; was released in several different forms. The
   51 T:0000                                    ; one reproduced by this source assembly file is
   52 T:0000                                    ; the main-board ROM form, which appeared in the
   53 T:0000                                    ; Apple ][ plus ROM at $D000-$F7FF.
   54 T:0000                                    ;
   55 T:0000                                    ; --------------------------------

